    "text": "Thomas Langley, District 1 Commissioner | Cass County\nThomas Langley, District 1 Commissioner | Cass County\nAn audit of randomly chosen precincts from the November 4, 2025 Special Election is scheduled for December 10, 2025. The process will begin at 9 a.m. in room 140 of the Cass County Building, located at 120 N. Broadway, Cassopolis, Michigan.\nThe audit is part of standard procedures to ensure the accuracy and integrity of election results. Random selection of precincts is a common practice used by counties across Michigan to verify that votes are counted correctly and that election processes comply with state regulations.\nAudits like this are open to the public and allow for transparency in how elections are managed within Cass County.",
